        ("Add a method `has(name)` returning True if the item is in stock with quantity > 0, and use it inside `remove` to raise KeyError('unknown item') when the item is absent (instead of the insufficient stock error).",
         "inv=Inventory(); inv.add('a',1); assert inv.has('a') and not inv.has('z')\ntry:\n    inv.remove('z',1); raise SystemExit(1)\nexcept KeyError as e: assert 'unknown item' in str(e)\ntry:\n    inv.remove('a',5); raise SystemExit(1)\nexcept ValueError: pass"),
        ("Make `restock` skip empty-string names and return the new total only counting what was added in this call.",
         "inv=Inventory(); inv.add('x',10)\nassert restock(inv,['a','','b'],2)==4\nassert inv.total()==14"),
        ("Make `dump` return the items sorted by quantity descending (ties by name) as a JSON list of [name, qty] pairs instead of an object.",
         "inv=Inventory(); inv.add('b',1); inv.add('a',1); inv.add('c',5)\nimport json\nassert json.loads(inv.dump())==[['c',5],['a',1],['b',1]]"),
        ("Add a class method `from_dict(cls, d)` that builds an Inventory from a name->qty dict (skipping non-positive quantities).",
